Good.

273
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:33,570
If there's nothing else.

274
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:36,810
There is another matter, Your Grace.

275
00:24:36,810 --> 00:24:39,530
Something so urgent I couldn't trust the words to a raven.

276
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:42,390
You once charged me with finding Arya Stark.

277
00:24:42,430 --> 00:24:44,160
To my shame, I failed you.

278
00:24:45,570 --> 00:24:47,720
But I have found Sansa Stark.

279
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:52,530
Alive and well and home again

280
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:54,600
living at Winterfell.

281
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:56,140
That's not possible.

282
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:58,350
My sources are well placed.

283
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:01,980
They tell me Roose Bolton plans to

284
00:25:01,980 --> 00:25:04,270
marry her to his son Ramsay,

285
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:07,320
A bastard recently legitimized by King Tommen.

286
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:11,030
Roose Bolton is Warden of the North by the grace of my father.

287
00:25:11,030 --> 00:25:15,110
Indeed, his reward for stabbing his own king in the heart.

288
00:25:16,220 --> 00:25:18,760
We were fools to trust a Turncloak.

289
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,990
Marrying his son to the last of the Starks

290
00:25:20,990 --> 00:25:22,780
gives him more legitimacy in the north

291
00:25:22,790 --> 00:25:25,150
than an alliance with a hated southern house.

292
00:25:25,150 --> 00:25:28,280
I will skin him and his bastard

293
00:25:28,280 --> 00:25:30,310
like that wretch on their bloody sigil.

294
00:25:30,310 --> 00:25:32,070
I would counsel patience, Your Grace.

295
00:25:32,070 --> 00:25:33,240
Patience?

296
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:35,400
Sansa helped murder my son.

297
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:36,830
Roose Bolton is a traitor.

298
00:25:36,830 --> 00:25:38,880
Stannis Baratheon is also a traitor,

299
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,870
marching with his army on Winterfell.

300
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:42,860
Let Stannis and Roose battle.

301
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:45,680
Let the enemies of the throne slaughter each other.

302
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:46,850
And when they're done,

303
00:25:46,850 --> 00:25:49,290
seize Winterfell from whichever thief survives.

304
00:25:49,290 --> 00:25:51,930
Winterfell is 1,000 miles away from here.

305
00:25:52,290 --> 00:25:54,290
The weather has already begun to turn.

306
00:25:54,290 --> 00:25:56,680
That is why it is critical to strike soon

307
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:59,160
while the victor still licks his wounds.

308
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:03,610
Surely your uncle Kevan could muster a force.

309
00:26:03,610 --> 00:26:06,990
My uncle Kevan has all the courage of a kitchen mouse.

310
00:26:06,990 --> 00:26:08,280
Ser Jaime, then.

311
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:10,930
Jaime's away on a sensitive diplomatic mission.

312
00:26:11,760 --> 00:26:13,700
I have no idea when he'll be back.

313
00:26:14,010 --> 00:26:15,590
Perhaps I can help.

314
00:26:16,690 --> 00:26:17,600
The knights of the Vale

315
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:19,530
are some of the best fighters in Westeros,

316
00:26:19,690 --> 00:26:22,120
trained to battle in the ice and the snow.

317
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,720
Forgive me, Lord Baelish,

318
00:26:25,050 --> 00:26:28,000
You have a reputation as a moneylender and a brothel keeper,

319
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,900
not a military man.

320
00:26:29,900 --> 00:26:32,000
You wouldn't risk a single Lannister soldier

321
00:26:32,060 --> 00:26:34,520
or a single coin from the royal treasury.

322
00:26:35,290 --> 00:26:36,550
What do you have to lose?

323
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:38,580
A brothel keeper?

324
00:26:39,260 --> 00:26:40,550
And if you succeed?

325
00:26:40,610 --> 00:26:42,700
Name me Warden of the North.

326
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,370
I'll speak to the King this evening,

327
00:26:50,710 --> 00:26:52,590
have him issue a royal decree.

328
00:26:53,020 --> 00:26:55,670
I'll not rest until the lion flies over Winterfell.

329
00:26:55,890 --> 00:26:57,900
And I'll know you're a man of your word

330
00:26:58,070 --> 00:27:01,240
when I see Sansa Stark's head on a spike.

331
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:02,420
As I said...

332
00:27:03,170 --> 00:27:04,970
I live to serve.

333
00:27:11,260 --> 00:27:13,610
I'm going to ask him tomorrow.

334
00:27:15,170 --> 00:27:17,250
- What if he says no? - He won't.

335
00:27:17,330 --> 00:27:18,840
We've waited long enough.

336
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,560
I want you to be my wife.

337
00:27:22,130 --> 00:27:23,250
Now.

338
00:27:25,450 --> 00:27:26,380
What is it?

339
00:27:26,540 --> 00:27:29,770
Do you want to marry me because our families arranged it?

340
00:27:29,770 --> 00:27:31,000
or do you...

341
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:41,840
We can't. Not yet.

342
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:42,850
Why not?

343
00:27:42,850 --> 00:27:44,940
You know why not. Someone will see.

344
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:47,060
You are going to be my wife.

345
00:27:47,490 --> 00:27:51,080
I am going to be your husband.

346
00:27:51,730 --> 00:27:54,220
We're allowed to walk through the gardens together.

347
00:27:54,810 --> 00:27:57,340
How many other girls have you walked through these gardens?

348
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:02,700
I like the way your eyes go squinty when you're jealous.

349
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:05,760
They do not go squinty and you didn't answer the question.

350
00:28:06,390 --> 00:28:08,220
They make a lovely couple.

351
00:28:08,790 --> 00:28:11,240
A Lannister and a Martell.

352
00:28:12,230 --> 00:28:15,180
They have no idea how dangerous that is.

353
00:28:15,650 --> 00:28:17,180
We must protect them.

354
00:28:17,450 --> 00:28:19,230
Yes, my prince.

355
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:23,970
You haven't had to use that axe of yours in a long time.

356
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:27,500
I hope you remember how.

357
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:29,660
I remember how.

358
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:36,280
*The Dornishman's wife was as fair as the sun,*

359
00:28:36,280 --> 00:28:40,880
*and her kisses were warmer than spring.*

360
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:45,740
*But the Dornishman's blade was made of black steel,*

361
00:28:45,780 --> 00:28:49,980
*and its kiss was a terrible thing.*

362
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:54,600
*The Dornishman's wife would sing as she bathed,*

363
00:28:54,740 --> 00:28:56,870
*in a voice that was sweet as a peach.*

364
00:28:56,870 --> 00:28:58,390
All right, that's enough.

365
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:00,230
I'm coming to the best part.

366
00:29:00,790 --> 00:29:02,120
We're trying to blend in.

367
00:29:02,720 --> 00:29:04,640
Don't want everyone in Dorne to hear your accent.

368
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:06,580
This song really is all about the ending.

369
00:29:06,580 --> 00:29:08,870
It can wait. There.

370
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,210
That's the Water Gardens.

371
00:29:14,310 --> 00:29:16,580
And once we've got the princess, then what?

372
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:20,640
I like to improvise.

373
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:24,000
That explains the golden hand.

374
00:29:44,180 --> 00:29:48,030
- Unbowed. - Unbent. - Unbroken.

375
00:29:50,020 --> 00:29:51,220
For Oberyn.

376
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:52,930
For Oberyn.

377
00:30:32,460 --> 00:30:34,230
Well, she's made herself at home.

378
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:41,440
Myrcella.

379
00:30:44,970 --> 00:30:46,220
Uncle Jaime?

380
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,040
I...

381
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:51,190
I don't understand. What are you doing here?

382
00:30:51,210 --> 00:30:52,230
Let's speak in private.

383
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:56,660
- I am Trystane Martell. - Trystane is my intended.

384
00:30:57,030 --> 00:30:59,340
Excellent. Good to meet you.

385
00:30:59,340 --> 00:31:00,840
We weren't expecting you, Lord Jaime.

386
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:03,340
Why don't you let them have some time alone, son?

387
00:31:08,820 --> 00:31:10,610
Let's not do something stupid.

388
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,160
That was something stupid.

389
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:18,690
We have to go, Myrcella, now.

390
00:31:18,690 --> 00:31:20,620
- You hurt him! - He'll be fine, I promise.

391
00:31:20,620 --> 00:31:21,730
But we have to--

392
00:31:26,140 --> 00:31:27,740
Oh, for fuck's sake.

393
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:11,310
Take her!

394
00:32:14,030 --> 00:32:15,800
- You're coming with me. - I don't want to.

395
00:32:15,810 --> 00:32:17,720
I wasn't asking, princess.

396
00:32:25,910 --> 00:32:27,210
Ah! Drop your weapons!

397
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,360
I am Obara Sand.

398
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:40,270
Daughter of Oberyn Martell.

399
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:43,750
I fight for Dorne. Who do you fight for?

400
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:45,690
Drop your weapons.

401
00:33:03,730 --> 00:33:06,800
When you were whole, it would have been a good fight.

402
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:19,380
You fight pretty good for a little girl.

403
00:33:46,530 --> 00:33:47,910
Halt!

404
00:33:51,030 --> 00:33:54,070
Oh, you can smell the shit from five miles away.

405
00:33:54,980 --> 00:33:56,820
Well, why have we stopped? Go on.

406
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:03,480
Rumors and gossip, that's all they've got.

407
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:05,180
It's theater, nothing more.

408
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:08,780
If they arrested all the pillow biters in King's Landing,

409
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:11,720
there'd be no room left in the dungeons for anyone else.

410
00:34:11,720 --> 00:34:13,420
Everyone knew about him and Renly.

411
00:34:13,610 --> 00:34:14,960
Renly Baratheon shagged

412
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:17,190
half the stable boys in the seven kingdoms.

413
00:34:17,190 --> 00:34:19,220
Everyone knew, no one cared.

414
00:34:19,220 --> 00:34:20,570
But he was the King's brother.

415
00:34:20,570 --> 00:34:22,490
And Loras is the Queen's brother.

416
00:34:22,490 --> 00:34:25,070
No, no, no, no. This is unacceptable.

417
00:34:25,070 --> 00:34:27,170
- Cersei's behind it. - Yeah, of course she is.

418
00:34:27,170 --> 00:34:29,450
She wants to drag our name through the dirt,

419
00:34:29,450 --> 00:34:31,090
put us in our place.

420
00:34:31,490 --> 00:34:33,400
Get some rest, dear. You look appalling.

421
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:35,420
Let me deal with Cersei Lannister.

422
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:45,270
Your grace, I have travelled a long way.

423
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,660
You must be exhausted.

424
00:34:50,290 --> 00:34:53,040
Put the pen down, dear. We both know you're not writing anything.

425
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:56,410
Ah, yes. The famously tart-tongued Queen of Thorns.

426
00:34:56,410 --> 00:34:59,440
And the famous tart Queen Cersei.

427
00:35:03,850 --> 00:35:04,840
I beg your pardon?

428
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:08,750
I know you're behind this absurd incarceration of my grandson.

429
00:35:09,230 --> 00:35:10,870
If you apologize for that comment, perhaps I'll--

430
00:35:10,870 --> 00:35:14,130
You'll get your apology when I get Loras.

431
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:16,870
I was as shocked as anyone

432
00:35:16,890 --> 00:35:19,240
when the Faith arrested Ser Loras.

433
00:35:19,940 --> 00:35:22,100
I have no love for these fanatics,

434
00:35:22,370 --> 00:35:24,170
but what can a Queen Mother do?

435
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:28,350
Has the Crown suddenly stopped needing

436
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:31,790
the troops, gold, and wheat my house supplies?

437
00:35:31,790 --> 00:35:33,010
I can assure you,

438
00:35:33,660 --> 00:35:35,720
our alliance with house Tyrell remains--

439
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:37,180
Do you expect the alliance to continue

440
00:35:37,180 --> 00:35:39,890
after you've thrown our future into prison?

441
00:35:41,290 --> 00:35:42,590
As I said,

442
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:44,810
I didn't imprison anyone.

443
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:46,680
As for your veiled threats--

444
00:35:46,740 --> 00:35:48,030
What veil?

445
00:35:50,120 --> 00:35:51,300
The Lannister-Tyrell alliance

446
00:35:51,300 --> 00:35:54,240
brought peace to a war-torn country.

447
00:35:54,700 --> 00:35:55,410
Do you really want to see

448
00:35:55,410 --> 00:35:58,100
the Seven Kingdoms slide back into warfare?

449
00:36:01,140 --> 00:36:03,020
I didn't trust your father.

450
00:36:03,620 --> 00:36:05,650
I didn't particularly like him.

451
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:08,980
But I respected him. He was no fool.

452
00:36:09,290 --> 00:36:12,810
He understood that sometimes we must work with our rivals

453
00:36:12,820 --> 00:36:14,610
rather than destroy them.

454
00:36:14,630 --> 00:36:16,600
House Lannister has no rival.

455
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:22,370
The High Septon has called for an inquest, not a trial.

456
00:36:22,490 --> 00:36:23,990
Just a small hearing to determine

457
00:36:23,990 --> 00:36:27,130
whether the charges against Loras have merit,

458
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:28,610
which I'm sure they don't.

459
00:36:29,050 --> 00:36:32,580
Loras will be freed, our happy alliance will continue...

460
00:36:34,230 --> 00:36:37,100
And we'll forget this unfortunate conversation ever happened.

461
00:36:39,190 --> 00:36:41,040
Good day, Lady Olenna.

462
00:36:59,860 --> 00:37:02,960
You are aware of the rumors concerning you and Renly?

463
00:37:04,310 --> 00:37:06,410
I don't pay attention to rumors.

464
00:37:06,910 --> 00:37:09,860
You were said to be despondent when he died.

465
00:37:10,510 --> 00:37:13,560
Witnesses state that you refused to leave his bedside

466
00:37:13,560 --> 00:37:16,050
even as Stannis's army closed in.

467
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:20,510
He was my friend. He was my king.

468
00:37:21,070 --> 00:37:22,940
Wasn't Joffrey your king?

469
00:37:23,230 --> 00:37:25,650
He was anointed by the Seven, not Renly.

470
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:30,350
I was wrong to support Renly's claim, I know that.

471
00:37:31,610 --> 00:37:33,460
But I was forgiven by Joffrey.

472
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:36,510
I fought for him at the battle of Blackwater.

473
00:37:36,610 --> 00:37:39,340
Yes, wearing Renly's armor.

474
00:37:40,570 --> 00:37:42,110
Why does it matter what I wore?

475
00:37:42,110 --> 00:37:44,290
Do you deny all the charges against you?

476
00:37:45,260 --> 00:37:46,620
Fornication.

477
00:37:47,250 --> 00:37:49,560
Buggery. Blasphemy.

478
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:51,050
Of course I deny them.

479
00:37:51,050 --> 00:37:53,190
You never lay with Renly Baratheon?

480
00:37:53,580 --> 00:37:54,750
Never.

481
00:37:55,210 --> 00:37:57,210
Nor any other man?

482
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:59,310
Never.

483
00:38:01,690 --> 00:38:03,990
That will be all, Ser Loras.

484
00:38:11,450 --> 00:38:14,050
Well, I think that's quite enough of that.

485
00:38:14,050 --> 00:38:16,750
The Faith calls Queen Margaery forward.

486
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:18,600
You call me forward?

487
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:21,170
Yes, we have some questions for you.

488
00:38:21,980 --> 00:38:24,720
- I am the Queen. - You are.

489
00:38:25,100 --> 00:38:27,390
And according to the law of the Seven,

490
00:38:27,390 --> 00:38:29,980
neither kings nor queens are exempt

491
00:38:29,980 --> 00:38:32,870
from testimony at a holy inquest.

492
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:54,270
How do you respond to these charges against your brother?

493
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:56,210
They are lies.

494
00:38:56,460 --> 00:38:58,200
- All of them? - All of them.

495
00:38:58,680 --> 00:38:59,980
Queen Margaery,

496
00:39:01,170 --> 00:39:02,580
in the presence of the gods,

497
00:39:02,580 --> 00:39:04,830
do you swear that your brother is innocent

498
00:39:04,830 --> 00:39:06,530
of these charges against him

499
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:08,480
to the best of your knowledge?

500
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:10,180
Yes, I swear it.

501
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:13,890
Thank you, your Grace.

502
00:39:39,570 --> 00:39:40,860
Do you know this man?

503
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,530
Yes, very well.

504
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:47,540
He is Ser Loras Tyrell, heir to Highgarden.

505
00:39:48,350 --> 00:39:49,950
How did you come to meet?

506
00:39:50,690 --> 00:39:52,410
I squired for him.

507
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:54,650
He took a liking to me.

508
00:39:54,740 --> 00:39:57,260
He summoned me to his chamber the first day we met.

509
00:39:59,330 --> 00:40:02,190
And what occurred in his chamber?

510
00:40:02,460 --> 00:40:07,060
We engaged in intimate relations.

511
00:40:07,660 --> 00:40:09,100
You lay with him?

512
00:40:09,260 --> 00:40:10,770
That night and many others.

513
00:40:10,770 --> 00:40:13,470
Liar. He's a liar.

514
00:40:14,210 --> 00:40:16,650
Is there anyone else who can support your claim?

515
00:40:17,330 --> 00:40:18,180
Yes.

516
00:40:19,130 --> 00:40:20,710
Yes, Queen Margaery.

517
00:40:21,940 --> 00:40:25,230
She walked in on us once not long ago.

518
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,980
She didn't seem surprised.

519
00:40:28,100 --> 00:40:31,650
This testimony is an insult to a great house.

520
00:40:31,780 --> 00:40:35,120
Why should the Faith or anyone else take the word of a squire

521
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:36,520
over the heir to Highgarden?

522
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:38,290
He has a birthmark, your Grace.

523
00:40:39,100 --> 00:40:41,090
Quite high on his thigh.

524
00:40:41,850 --> 00:40:44,500
Wine-colored and roughly the shape of Dorne.

525
00:40:45,180 --> 00:40:46,990
No! Liar!

526
00:40:49,590 --> 00:40:52,850
What are you doing? Let us pass.

527
00:40:52,850 --> 00:40:55,550
The Faith is satisfied there is enough evidence

528
00:40:55,550 --> 00:40:57,350
to bring a formal trial

529
00:40:57,990 --> 00:40:59,270
for Ser Loras

530
00:41:00,230 --> 00:41:01,510
and Queen Margaery.

531
00:41:01,520 --> 00:41:02,370
What?

532
00:41:03,110 --> 00:41:04,820
Bearing false witness before the gods

533
00:41:04,820 --> 00:41:07,090
is as grave a sin as any, my lady.

534
00:41:08,030 --> 00:41:08,940
Take her.

535
00:41:09,340 --> 00:41:12,020
No. Tommen.

536
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:13,220
Tommen!

537
00:41:15,070 --> 00:41:17,400
You can't do this. I am the queen.

538
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:19,810
Tommen! Tommen!

539
00:41:20,910 --> 00:41:22,360
I am your queen. How dare you?

540
00:41:22,360 --> 00:41:23,820
Take your hands off me!

541
00:41:25,870 --> 00:41:26,840
Tommen!

542
00:41:50,450 --> 00:41:51,500
What do you want?

543
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:55,140
Lord Ramsay sent me to draw you a bath, my lady.

544
00:41:56,150 --> 00:41:57,670
You want to be clean and fresh

545
00:41:57,680 --> 00:41:59,350
for your new husband, don't you?

546
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:18,140
You're so beautiful,

547
00:42:19,300 --> 00:42:21,190
but you need to keep him happy.

548
00:42:22,310 --> 00:42:25,160
Ramsay gets bored easily.

549
00:42:26,910 --> 00:42:28,700
You don't want to end up like--

550
00:42:30,470 --> 00:42:32,900
well, like the others.

551
00:42:34,150 --> 00:42:35,220
What others?

552
00:42:35,900 --> 00:42:37,390
I shouldn't gossip.

553
00:42:37,810 --> 00:42:39,680
Oh, it's good to see the red again.

554
00:42:40,830 --> 00:42:42,350
No point hiding anymore.

555
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:43,720
What others?

556
00:42:43,950 --> 00:42:46,600
Let's see, there was kyra

557
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:48,410
the blacksmith's daughter.

558
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:51,290
She was tall like you, lovely figure.

559
00:42:51,290 --> 00:42:56,000
But she talked and talked and talked

560
00:42:57,170 --> 00:42:58,770
and Ramsay grew tired of that.

561
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:01,320
Then there was Violet.

562
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:04,270
She had gorgeous blonde hair.

563
00:43:04,270 --> 00:43:07,360
But she got pregnant.

564
00:43:07,360 --> 00:43:10,110
And, well, that was boring.

565
00:43:11,260 --> 00:43:13,840
Then Tansy.

566
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:15,450
Such a sweet girl.

567
00:43:15,920 --> 00:43:20,480
Of course, sweet girls get a bit dull

568
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,630
after a while, don't they?

569
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:25,420
Ramsay let me come with him on that hunt.

570
00:43:25,450 --> 00:43:26,440
Hunt?

571
00:43:30,060 --> 00:43:33,590
Have you ever seen a body after the dogs have been at it?

572
00:43:34,820 --> 00:43:36,530
Not so pretty.

573
00:43:38,900 --> 00:43:41,190
But, well, it's your wedding day.

574
00:43:42,090 --> 00:43:44,120
Why am I talking about such things?

575
00:43:46,920 --> 00:43:48,330
What was your name again?

576
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:49,450
Myranda.

577
00:43:52,220 --> 00:43:54,540
And how long have you loved him, Myranda?

578
00:43:58,740 --> 00:44:01,710
Did you imagine that he would be with you forever, is that it?

579
00:44:01,720 --> 00:44:03,450
And I came along and ruined it.

580
00:44:06,780 --> 00:44:09,260
I'm Sansa Stark of Winterfell.

581
00:44:10,470 --> 00:44:14,300
This is my home and you can't frighten me.

582
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,310
Are you done with your bath, my lady?

583
00:44:24,100 --> 00:44:25,950
Go. I can finish on my own.

584
00:44:52,250 --> 00:44:53,170
Yes?

585
00:45:02,530 --> 00:45:05,340
I've come to escort you to the godswood, my lady.

586
00:45:09,960 --> 00:45:13,210
If you please, my lady, will you take my arm?

587
00:45:13,260 --> 00:45:14,020
No.

588
00:45:16,300 --> 00:45:18,910
Lord Ramsay, he said I'm to take your arm.

589
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:20,430
I'm not touching you.

590
00:45:22,630 --> 00:45:23,570
Please.

591
00:45:24,880 --> 00:45:26,050
He'll punish me.

592
00:45:28,330 --> 00:45:30,650
You think I care what he does to you?

593
00:46:48,460 --> 00:46:50,940
Who comes before the old gods this night?

594
00:46:52,250 --> 00:46:55,270
Sansa of the house Stark

595
00:46:56,670 --> 00:46:58,240
comes here to be wed.

596
00:47:00,380 --> 00:47:04,260
A woman grown, trueborn and noble.

597
00:47:05,350 --> 00:47:07,890
She comes to beg the blessings of the gods.

598
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:12,530
Who comes to claim her?

599
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:23,550
Ramsay of house Bolton.

600
00:47:24,890 --> 00:47:27,390
Heir to the Dreadfort and winterfell.

601
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:30,900
Who gives her?

602
00:47:34,620 --> 00:47:39,150
Theon of house Greyjoy, who was--

603
00:47:43,890 --> 00:47:45,690
who was her father's ward.

604
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:51,320
Lady Sansa, will you take this man?

605
00:48:21,390 --> 00:48:22,680
I take this man.

606
00:48:54,880 --> 00:48:56,800
Are you pleased, my lady?

607
00:48:59,740 --> 00:49:02,320
Good. I want you to be happy.

608
00:49:12,900 --> 00:49:15,170
My father said you're still a virgin.

609
00:49:20,800 --> 00:49:23,470
- Uh, yes. - Why?

610
00:49:27,650 --> 00:49:29,570
Why are you still a virgin?

611
00:49:31,370 --> 00:49:32,780
Afraid of dwarves?

612
00:49:34,530 --> 00:49:36,540
Lord-- lord Tyrion was kind.

613
00:49:36,540 --> 00:49:39,960
He was gentle. He never touched me.

614
00:49:41,990 --> 00:49:43,500
You're not lying to me?

615
00:49:43,930 --> 00:49:44,930
No, my lord.

616
00:49:44,930 --> 00:49:47,550
Lying to your husband on his wedding night,

617
00:49:48,460 --> 00:49:51,220
that would be a bad way to start a marriage.

618
00:49:56,410 --> 00:49:58,150
We're man and wife now.

619
00:49:59,370 --> 00:50:01,060
We should be honest with each other.

620
00:50:01,970 --> 00:50:03,010
Don't you think?

621
00:50:04,570 --> 00:50:05,480
Yes.

622
00:50:16,450 --> 00:50:17,320
Good.

623
00:50:20,570 --> 00:50:22,050
Take off your clothes.

624
00:50:26,050 --> 00:50:27,440
Oh, no, no, no.

625
00:50:28,940 --> 00:50:30,620
You stay here, Reek.

626
00:50:31,470 --> 00:50:32,780
You watch.

627
00:50:45,840 --> 00:50:47,850
Do I need to ask a second time?

628
00:50:48,490 --> 00:50:50,380
I hate asking a second time.

629
00:51:18,910 --> 00:51:19,990
Reek...

630
00:51:21,060 --> 00:51:22,800
I told you to watch.

631
00:51:28,970 --> 00:51:31,300
You've known Sansa since she was a girl.

632
00:51:33,200 --> 00:51:34,920
Now watch her become a woman.

